# A crash dump. When a program crashes inside a Linux container, the
# kernel can write its memory to a file named core (or core.<pid>) in the
# working directory, which is the project root. The leading slash keeps
# the rule at the root so a real folder named core deeper in the project
# is still tracked.
/core
/core.[0-9]*
